  "details": "<p>The bronze bowl mentioned above belonged to the ninth century B.C. Babylonian ruler Marduk-z\u0101kir-\u0161umi I, a contemporary of the well-known Assyrian king Shalmaneser III.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Zalu Ab (also Romanized as Z\u0101l\u016b \u0100b and Z\u0101l\u016b\u0101b) is a village in Zalu Ab Rural District, in the Central District of Ravansar County, Kermanshah Province, Iran. Several ancient objects, including a bronze bowl of a Chaldean tribal leader, are reported to have been discovered in this rural Iranian village.",
